Cell["\<\
Check: {True, n, True}: prefix and back returns the same expression for the \
three examples and for every one of the n random expressions that came out \
well formed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c69b6769-7d0a-479e-be6a-6282ec120053"],

Cell["4. Counting trees and expressions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"82138711-a8db-4b6a-875c-50d423e414c1"],

Cell["\<\
To sample fairly one must first count. Let D(e, n) be the number of ways to \
complete a tree that still has e empty slots and n internal nodes to place. \
The first empty slot is a leaf, a unary node or a binary node (Appendix C of \
the paper):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a59840f9-8c80-47a4-b57b-9d0e9db2f766"],

Cell["\<\
D(0, n) = 0 (n > 0),    D(e, 0) = 1,    D(e, n) = D(e \[Minus] 1, n) + D(e, n \
\[Minus] 1) + D(e + 1, n \[Minus] 1)\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"bf41a124-1944-4e0d-badc-0af4f1697106"],

Cell["\<\
D(1, n) counts whole trees with n internal nodes. With binary nodes only, the \
middle term is dropped and D(1, n) is the Catalan number C\:2099; with unary \
and binary nodes it is the large Schr\[ODoubleDot]der number S\:2099.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b07099b-afb3-44e0-a1b5-f1245f9079b4"],

Cell["4.1 Worked by hand: the six trees with two internal nodes", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7f1db69e-1bb7-477e-8d64-dc79352c2fd6"],

Cell["\<\
Write u for a unary node, b for a binary node and \[Bullet] for a leaf. The \
trees with two internal nodes, in prefix order, are u u \[Bullet], u b \
\[Bullet] \[Bullet], b u \[Bullet] \[Bullet], b \[Bullet] u \[Bullet], b b \
\[Bullet] \[Bullet] \[Bullet] and b \[Bullet] b \[Bullet] \[Bullet]. That is \
6 = S\:2082. By the recurrence: D(1, 2) = D(0, 2) + D(1, 1) + D(2, 1) = 0 + 2 \
+ 4 = 6, where D(1, 1) = 2 (u \[Bullet] and b \[Bullet] \[Bullet]) and D(2, \
1) = D(1, 1) + D(2, 0) + D(3, 0) = 2 + 1 + 1 = 4.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"3e3d5092-53e4-4d67-899d-54ac832a90ba"],

