Cell["\<\
Check: {True, True, True}. The counts agree with Catalan for n \[LessEqual] \
12, with Schr\[ODoubleDot]der (the paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Equation 1) for n \
\[LessEqual] 12, and with the trees listed one by one for n \[LessEqual] 7.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9789a080-69eb-45c1-882e-669180b0ec62"],

Cell["4.2 Counting expressions, and a correction to Equation 2", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"35ab7ffe-2f77-4f97-abd0-47a8381a2044"],

Cell["\<\
An expression is a tree whose leaves take one of L values, unary nodes one of \
p\:2081 operators and binary nodes one of p\:2082. So each tree counts \
L^leaves p\:2081^unary p\:2082^binary times. The paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
Equation 2 gives a recurrence for the total E\:2099. As printed it ends in \
\[Minus]p\:2081(n \[Minus] 2)E\:2099\:208b\:2082. Expanding (1 \[Minus] p\
\:2081z)\.b2 in its generating function (Appendix B) gives p\:2081\.b2 there \
instead. The two agree only when p\:2081 is 0 or 1, which are the cases the \
paper checks against Equation 1 and the Catalan numbers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a33b73a9-5e4e-47c0-8a63-149bc16fc3f7"],

Cell["\<\
corrected:   (n + 1) E\:2099 = (p\:2081 + 2 L p\:2082)(2n \[Minus] 1) E\:2099\
\:208b\:2081 \[Minus] p\:2081\.b2 (n \[Minus] 2) E\:2099\:208b\:2082,     E\
\:2080 = L,   E\:2081 = p\:2081L + p\:2082L\.b2\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"9f434935-e66a-4cf9-8744-f21a0aa31ba7"],

