Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True", ",", "True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[12]=",ExpressionUUID->"262c32d5-240c-4ea7-833c-435cf904926f"],

Cell["\<\
Check: {True, True, True, True}. The corrected form equals the count of every \
tree; the printed form first differs at n = 3 when p\:2081 = 3, and is right \
throughout when p\:2081 = 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51e422a4-6daa-4fcc-a390-a017ba2a441c"],

Cell["\<\
Why the square: the generating function satisfies E(z) = L + p\:2081zE(z) + p\
\:2082zE(z)\.b2, so 2p\:2082zE = 1 \[Minus] p\:2081z \[Minus] \[Sqrt]((1 \
\[Minus] p\:2081z)\.b2 \[Minus] 4Lp\:2082z). Under the root, (1 \[Minus] p\
\:2081z)\.b2 \[Minus] 4Lp\:2082z = 1 \[Minus] 2(p\:2081 + 2Lp\:2082)z + p\
\:2081\.b2z\.b2. The paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Appendix B writes p\:2081z\.b2 \
for the last term, and the p\:2081 carries into Equation 2.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"df3e3884-47cb-4ff9-85c0-96be257310f0"],

