Cell["Check: {5.43 \[Times] 10\.b3\.b3, 33}.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b7ea05c8-cf72-48ad-9afd-be306f096ad7"],

Cell["5. Sampling trees uniformly", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"236f1592-3ac2-4cb6-a0e6-ae30b77fd644"],

Cell["\<\
A naive recursive generator (binary or unary with fixed probabilities, then a \
random split of the remaining nodes) favours some shapes. The paper samples \
every tree with n internal nodes equally often. Start with one empty slot, e \
= 1. Choose the position k and arity a of the next internal node with\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b04b4b9c-c3ba-4afc-9ef7-7c4f88c5bdcd"],

Cell["\<\
P(k, unary) = D(e \[Minus] k, n \[Minus] 1) / D(e, n),     P(k, binary) = D(e \
\[Minus] k + 1, n \[Minus] 1) / D(e, n),     k = 0, \[Ellipsis], e \[Minus] 1\
\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"dce616f0-a38e-4460-a463-126aab9cd000"],

Cell["\<\
The k slots before it become leaves. Then e becomes e \[Minus] k (unary) or e \
\[Minus] k + 1 (binary), and n falls by 1. The tree comes out in prefix order.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b44b3042-1f76-49fb-88e7-653221d3ad62"],

Cell["5.1 Worked by hand: the first choice for n = 2", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"55621f08-733c-41f8-9311-6a1f12021b82"],

Cell["\<\
With e = 1 only k = 0 is possible. P(0, unary) = D(1, 1)/D(1, 2) = 2/6 = 1/3 \
and P(0, binary) = D(2, 1)/D(1, 2) = 4/6 = 2/3. That matches the list of \
\[Section]4.1: of the six trees, two start with u and four with b. A fair \
first choice is exactly the fraction of trees that start that way.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"49ffbad0-d6eb-4e83-9e5e-2d3e5afd8790"],

